<p>Israel said on April 5 that it planned to strike a Lebanon-Syria border crossing and urged residents to evacuate. The Israeli military also said it had begun striking Hezbollah infrastructure in Beirut after destroying a bridge in eastern Lebanon to block crossings by Hezbollah members. The moves are part of what Israel says is a campaign against Hezbollah infrastructure. The fighting has deepened Lebanon’s displacement crisis. DW reported that more than 1.1 million Lebanese have fled their homes. In earlier coverage, The Hindu reported that tens of thousands fled Tyre after evacuation orders, while roughly 20,000 people remained there, including about 15,000 already displaced from nearby villages. El Pais said the war has imposed devastating costs on Lebanese civilians and reported that, despite earlier setbacks after the 2024 ceasefire, Hezbollah has kept capabilities that have complicated Israel’s campaign.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/aqQS0aJ-JoU5OGhMbYpkZjVggOUTDVxqP-WzrtD0atGGVha82XhXnPDdCvLsDG1pwgeUe6PAI2oY0juYciS8rgZNAe3vODycIHoN2qm6hlTg5B9MXHVFsKXp-RX7RPWS9YI_V_vTAo0g1c0Upboa4ymR9ps33_UkHGddQXYDz-LzSWSJD_BgR97x1aIOmV5Yso-icbBYdmW8r1HI4B54weXcO-LcKm_qeMLqSnZGukjco2Qxu8QaqXIhG86Qd4SCZx9TSXODUHJoknw0TmvzzCzU' alt='Scene from Tyre after Israeli strikes followed evacuation warnings.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Border route: Israel said it would strike a Lebanon-Syria border crossing and urged residents to leave immediately, increasing pressure on a key cross-border route.</li><li>Bridge strike: The Times of Israel reported that the Israeli military said it destroyed a bridge in eastern Lebanon to stop Hezbollah members from crossing, then launched strikes in Beirut.</li><li>Hezbollah status: El Pais reported that Hezbollah, weakened after the 2024 war and subsequent Israeli pressure, has nonetheless emerged stronger after the past month of fighting.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli military: The military said it had started striking Hezbollah infrastructure in Beirut and had destroyed a bridge in eastern Lebanon to prevent Hezbollah members from crossing. (<a href='https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/loud-explosions-heard-in-beirut-after-idf-announces-strikes-on-hezbollah-sites/'>Times of Israel</a>)</li><li>Displaced Lebanese civilians: DW focused on families uprooted by the fighting who are trying to preserve daily routines and some sense of normality despite losing their homes and stable living conditions. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/displaced-in-lebanon-lives-turned-upside-down/a-76662137'>DW</a>)</li><li>El Pais analysis: El Pais assessed that Israel is confronting Hezbollah capabilities it did not expect to remain intact, even after the 2024 ceasefire, regular strikes, and a Lebanese government disarmament push. (<a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-04-05/after-a-month-of-war-with-israel-hezbollah-emerges-strengthened-amid-the-pain-of-lebanese-civilians.html'>El Pais</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/displaced-in-lebanon-lives-turned-upside-down/a-76662137'>Displaced in Lebanon: &#x27;Lives turned upside down&#x27;</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-strikes-south-lebanons-tyre-after-issuing-evacuation-warnings/article70824363.ece'>Israel strikes south Lebanon’s Tyre after issuing evacuation warnings</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-04-05/after-a-month-of-war-with-israel-hezbollah-emerges-strengthened-amid-the-pain-of-lebanese-civilians.html'>After a month of war with Israel, Hezbollah emerges strengthened amid the pain of Lebanese civilians</a> - elpais.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/israel-says-will-strike-lebanon-syria-border-crossing'>Israel says will strike Lebanon-Syria border crossing</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/loud-explosions-heard-in-beirut-after-idf-announces-strikes-on-hezbollah-sites/'>The Israeli military says on Telegram that it has started striking Hezbollah infrastructure in Beirut after destroying a bridge in eastern Lebanon to prevent them from crossing.</a> - timesofisrael.com</li></ul>